From: Jorge Ramirez-Ortiz <jorge.ramirez@oss.qualcomm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: qcs6490-rb3gen2: keep rmtfs_mem

The RB3Gen2 board DTS deletes rmtfs_mem (rmtfs@9c900000, from kodiak.dtsi)
along with the other reserved-memory nodes it relocates, but never re-adds
it. Without the reserved region the qcom_rmtfs_mem driver creates no
/dev/qcom_rmtfs_mem* nodes, so rmtfs fails ("failed to open
/dev/qcom_rmtfs_mem1") and the ADSP protection domains never finish coming
up (ADSP FastRPC glink intent timeout). The 0x9c900000/0x280000 slot is
free in the board map and abuts adsp-rpc-remote-heap@9cb80000, so keep the
node by dropping its delete.

Signed-off-by: Jorge Ramirez-Ortiz <jorge.ramirez@oss.qualcomm.com>
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs6490-rb3gen2.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs6490-rb3gen2.dts
index 7591cb1ef..eb1aa1a2f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs6490-rb3gen2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs6490-rb3gen2.dts
@@ -22,7 +22,6 @@
 #include "qcs6490-audioreach.dtsi"
 
 /delete-node/ &ipa_fw_mem;
-/delete-node/ &rmtfs_mem;
 /delete-node/ &adsp_mem;
 /delete-node/ &cdsp_mem;
 /delete-node/ &video_mem;
